sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/blueprint-well-formed-a-flying-fish> a delphi:Hypothesis, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "The emitted blueprint for \"a flying-fish with enlarged pectoral fins that glides above the water\" is structurally well-formed (kernel-checked certificate)" ;
    dct:description "The blueprint the organism thread's tool emitted for \"a flying-fish with enlarged pectoral fins that glides above the water\" (Exocoetidae, NCBITaxon_76072; file organism-design/examples/a-flying-fish.json, sha256 c526294faebb6fcf791a8fcdc2bcc59beabe53af769842b6c29dccffca87bd6f) is well-formed under its own rules: its 674 part_of placements over 536 distinct terms all go strictly down in level, form no cycle, and lead every term to the body root; 1390 never_in_taxon statements reachable from kept terms name no taxon that contains Exocoetidae (containing taxa pinned from Ubergraph: 32), and 5435 in_taxon plus 64 stated_in_taxon statements all name containing taxa. Distinct terms per level: body 1, organ_system 13, organ 67, tissue 198, cell 257 (placements: body 1, organ_system 13, organ 68, tissue 250, cell 343). The Lean kernel evaluated the checker (Delphi.Blueprint.Certificates.aFlyingFish_check) and accepted Delphi.Blueprint.Certificates.aFlyingFish_wellFormed, Delphi.Blueprint.Certificates.aFlyingFish_counts and Delphi.Blueprint.Certificates.aFlyingFish_size with standard axioms only." ;
    delphi:context "Certificate generated 2026-10-31T16:25:12.265Z by lean/blueprint/certify.mjs from the blueprint file and lean/blueprint/data/a-flying-fish.taxon.json (sha256 823cbcc7dd577999c6b89587e844f9ec5dd36deb419c9aba35988e27e7472554; 57 SPARQL queries to https://ubergraph.apps.renci.org/sparql, retrieved 2026-10-31T16:21:27.666Z to 2026-10-31T16:21:31.689Z). Generic theory: lean/Delphi/Blueprint.lean. Lean leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; certificate compiled in 83.8 s." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/blueprint-certificate-a-flying-fish> ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/blueprint-well-formedness> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Every part_of edge goes from a strictly deeper level to a shallower one (Graph.LevelsDown), so the part_of relation is acyclic: no term is transitively part of itself (Graph.acyclic_of_levelsDown)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: The transitive closure of the stated edges is transitive and strictly decreases the level (Graph.transGen_trans, Graph.transGen_level_lt)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Every edge joins two nodes of the graph and every node other than the body root has a whole, hence every node reaches the body root: no orphans (Graph.rooted_of)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: No never_in_taxon statement pinned from Ubergraph on a kept term, a superclass or a whole names a taxon containing the blueprint taxon; every in_taxon and stated_in_taxon statement names a containing taxon (TaxonData.Ok)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Nodes are distinct terms (List.nodup_range) and the distinct counts per level are body 1, organ_system 13, organ 67, tissue 198, cell 257; the file holds 674 placements." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: That Uberon and the Cell Ontology are correct and that Ubergraph served their part_of, subClassOf, never_in_taxon and in_taxon statements correctly and completely on the retrieval dates; the graph and the taxon rows are data whose hashes and queries are pinned here." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: That the five levels are the right notion of depth; the theorems use only that edges strictly decrease it." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: 0 never_in_taxon row(s) whose object is not an NCBITaxon term are not representable in the checker and are listed in the taxon data file, not checked." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: Nothing about any organism: the certificate says the emitted structure is internally coherent under its own stated rules. It does not say the fish is real, that the anatomy is correct or complete, that any part was measured, or anything about a transition between forms." ;
    rdfs:comment "Does not establish: that Exocoetidae or any organism has these structures; that the anatomy is correct or complete; that Uberon, the Cell Ontology or Ubergraph are right; that any part was measured; or anything about a transition between forms. It establishes only that the emitted structure is internally coherent under its own stated rules, with the data pinned by hash. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated." ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-a-flying-fish> ;
    rdfs:comment "Related record: <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-a-flying-fish> is the organism thread's own record of this blueprint. This record is a citation of it, not a statement about its truth, and no support or derivation relation is asserted in either direction. The organism thread may attach this certificate as evidence from its side if it chooses; this record does not do so." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Certificates/AFlyingFish.lean>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Blueprint.lean>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/blueprint/certificates/a-flying-fish.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/organism-design/examples/a-flying-fish.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/#blueprint> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/blueprint-certificate-a-flying-fish> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted the well-formedness certificate of the \"a flying-fish with enlarged pectoral fins that glides above the water\" blueprint" ;
    dct:description "Delphi.Blueprint.Certificates.aFlyingFish_wellFormed := wellFormed_of_check _ _ Delphi.Blueprint.Certificates.aFlyingFish_check, where Delphi.Blueprint.Certificates.aFlyingFish_check is proved by decide +kernel on the literal graph (536 nodes, 674 edges) and taxon data (32 ancestors, 1390 never_in_taxon rows, 5435 in_taxon rows, 64 stated_in_taxon rows). #print axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. Blueprint file sha256 c526294faebb6fcf791a8fcdc2bcc59beabe53af769842b6c29dccffca87bd6f (built 2026-10-31T15:47:53.241Z); taxon data sha256 823cbcc7dd577999c6b89587e844f9ec5dd36deb419c9aba35988e27e7472554. Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs): [blueprint-closure-level-flipped] Statement changed to claim the level INCREASES along the part_of closure (level a < level b) instead of decreasing; acyclicity rests on this lemma, so the proof must fail. rejected. [blueprint-certificate-cycle] Data sabotaged: an edge making the body root part of node 1 is added to the certified edge list (an upward edge, closing a cycle through the root). The kernel-evaluated checker must reject it. rejected. [blueprint-certificate-excluded-taxon] Data sabotaged: a never_in_taxon row saying node 1 is never in Vertebrata (NCBITaxon 7742, an ancestor of Exocoetidae) is added. The checker must reject it. rejected." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/blueprint-well-formed-a-flying-fish> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the checker accepts the pinned data and that the generic theorems apply. It is not evidence about any organism." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/blueprint/certificates/a-flying-fish.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/blueprint/data/a-flying-fish.taxon.json> .
}

